d 'QUADRICEPS': module implementing positive-weight cubature rules for the Gaussian weight (ghpos) and the cube (lepos)
d
d     A cubature rule of degree p in d dimensions is a set of n
d nodes x_i in R^d and weights w_i > 0 such that sum_i w_i f(x_i)  
d  equals the integral of f against the weight function for every
d polynomial f of total degree at most p. The product of q-node   
d one-dimensional Gauss rules does this for p = 2q - 1 with q^d
d nodes. The rules stored in this package, the smallest   
d positive-weight rules known to the author, do it with far fewer:
d for example 244 nodes instead of 3125 for the Gaussian weight   
d at d = 5, q = 5. 
d
d KW: cubature rules
d KW: Gaussian weights
d KW: cube weights
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260925
d
d Author: Joris Pinkse,  Penn State University
d Support: email  pinkse@@gmail.com
d
f quadriceps.ado
f quadriceps.mata
f quadriceps.sthlp
F quadriceps_index.tsv
F quadriceps_rules.bin
f quadriceps_test.do
f ../g/ghpos.ado
f ../g/ghpos.sthlp
f ../l/lepos.ado
f ../l/lepos.sthlp
